{"id":"palladia-mors","name":"Palladia-Mors","type":"character","aliases":["Mors","Palladia"],"description":"Palladia-Mors is a vicious reddish-green elder dragon of Dominaria, mother of the Primeval Rith, who was put to sleep after the Battle at Mors Ridge.","pages":16,"first_seen":"2018-06-13","last_seen":"2018-08-08","description_citations":[{"source":"mtg-wiki","official":false,"publisher":"MTG Wiki contributors","work":"Palladia-Mors","series":"MTG Wiki","authors":[],"date":"","url":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Palladia-Mors","link":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Palladia-Mors","archived":null,"license":"CC BY-NC-SA 4.0","text":"\"Palladia-Mors\". MTG Wiki contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0."},{"source":"mtg-wiki","official":false,"publisher":"MTG Wiki contributors","work":"Rith","series":"MTG Wiki","authors":[],"date":"","url":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Rith","link":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Rith#:~:text=She%20is%20the%20daughter%20of%20Palladia%2DMors","archived":null,"license":"CC BY-NC-SA 4.0","text":"\"Rith\". MTG Wiki contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0."}],"bio":{"summary":{"text":"Palladia-Mors is a vicious reddish-green elder dragon of Dominaria, mother of the Primeval Rith, who was put to sleep after the Battle at Mors Ridge.","cites":["p:wiki/palladia-mors","rith-r1"],"links":["https://mtg.wiki/page/Palladia-Mors","https://mtg.wiki/page/Rith#:~:text=She%20is%20the%20daughter%20of%20Palladia%2DMors"],"citations":[{"source":"mtg-wiki","official":false,"publisher":"MTG Wiki contributors","work":"Palladia-Mors","series":"MTG Wiki","authors":[],"date":"","url":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Palladia-Mors","link":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Palladia-Mors","archived":null,"license":"CC BY-NC-SA 4.0","text":"\"Palladia-Mors\". MTG Wiki contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0."},{"source":"mtg-wiki","official":false,"publisher":"MTG Wiki contributors","work":"Rith","series":"MTG Wiki","authors":[],"date":"","url":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Rith","link":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Rith#:~:text=She%20is%20the%20daughter%20of%20Palladia%2DMors","archived":null,"license":"CC BY-NC-SA 4.0","text":"\"Rith\". MTG Wiki contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0."}]},"bio":[{"text":"In a vision she named herself with Arcades Sabboth and Chromium Rhuell when dragons woke from egg-stones, and she dismissed two weak eggs as useless before going hunting.","cites":["chronicle-bolas-twins-2018-06-13-e9","chronicle-bolas-twins-2018-06-13-e10"],"links":["https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/chronicle-bolas-twins-2018-06-13#:~:text=By%20naming%20itself%20it,of%20its%20own%20destiny.","https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/chronicle-bolas-twins-2018-06-13#:~:text=These%20two%20were%20too,wake%20up.%20Good%20riddance."],"citations":[{"source":"wizards","official":true,"publisher":"Wizards of the Coast","work":"Chronicle of Bolas: The Twins","series":"Magic Story","authors":["Kate Elliott"],"date":"2018-06-13","url":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/chronicle-bolas-twins-2018-06-13","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/chronicle-bolas-twins-2018-06-13#:~:text=By%20naming%20itself%20it,of%20its%20own%20destiny.","archived":null,"license":null,"text":"\"Chronicle of Bolas: The Twins\" by Kate Elliott. Magic Story, Wizards of the Coast, 13 Jun 2018."},{"source":"wizards","official":true,"publisher":"Wizards of the Coast","work":"Chronicle of Bolas: The Twins","series":"Magic Story","authors":["Kate Elliott"],"date":"2018-06-13","url":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/chronicle-bolas-twins-2018-06-13","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/chronicle-bolas-twins-2018-06-13#:~:text=These%20two%20were%20too,wake%20up.%20Good%20riddance.","archived":null,"license":null,"text":"\"Chronicle of Bolas: The Twins\" by Kate Elliott. Magic Story, Wizards of the Coast, 13 Jun 2018."}]},{"text":"She scorned the twins as runts, stole their kills and warned them that nearby humans took them for dragon hunters.","cites":["chronicle-bolas-first-lesson-2018-06-20-e10","chronicle-bolas-things-unseen-2018-06-27-e11"],"links":["https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/chronicle-bolas-first-lesson-2018-06-20#:~:text=You%27re%20so%20small%2C%20the,of%20you.%20Little%20runts.","https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/chronicle-bolas-things-unseen-2018-06-27#:~:text=Those%20humans%20have%20gotten,they%20are%20dragon%20hunters."],"citations":[{"source":"wizards","official":true,"publisher":"Wizards of the Coast","work":"Chronicle of Bolas: The First Lesson","series":"Magic Story","authors":["Kate Elliott"],"date":"2018-06-20","url":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/chronicle-bolas-first-lesson-2018-06-20","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/chronicle-bolas-first-lesson-2018-06-20#:~:text=You%27re%20so%20small%2C%20the,of%20you.%20Little%20runts.","archived":null,"license":null,"text":"\"Chronicle of Bolas: The First Lesson\" by Kate Elliott. Magic Story, Wizards of the Coast, 20 Jun 2018."},{"source":"wizards","official":true,"publisher":"Wizards of the Coast","work":"Chronicle of Bolas: Things Unseen","series":"Magic Story","authors":["Kate Elliott"],"date":"2018-06-27","url":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/chronicle-bolas-things-unseen-2018-06-27","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/chronicle-bolas-things-unseen-2018-06-27#:~:text=Those%20humans%20have%20gotten,they%20are%20dragon%20hunters.","archived":null,"license":null,"text":"\"Chronicle of Bolas: Things Unseen\" by Kate Elliott. Magic Story, Wizards of the Coast, 27 Jun 2018."}]},{"text":"Being impressionable, she was drawn into the Elder Dragon War that Nicol Bolas instigated by spreading lies among the dragon clans.","cites":["palladia-mors-e0","chronicle-bolas-blood-and-fire-2018-07-18-e18"],"links":["https://mtg.wiki/page/Palladia-Mors#:~:text=one%20of%20the%20first,the%20Elder%20Dragon%20War","https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/chronicle-bolas-blood-and-fire-2018-07-18#:~:text=The%20ease%20with%20which,purpose%20was%20surprisingly%20pleasurable."],"citations":[{"source":"mtg-wiki","official":false,"publisher":"MTG Wiki contributors","work":"Palladia-Mors","series":"MTG Wiki","authors":[],"date":"","url":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Palladia-Mors","link":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Palladia-Mors#:~:text=one%20of%20the%20first,the%20Elder%20Dragon%20War","archived":null,"license":"CC BY-NC-SA 4.0","text":"\"Palladia-Mors\", section \"Elder Dragon War\". MTG Wiki contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0."},{"source":"wizards","official":true,"publisher":"Wizards of the Coast","work":"Chronicle of Bolas: Blood and Fire","series":"Magic Story","authors":["Kate Elliott"],"date":"2018-07-18","url":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/chronicle-bolas-blood-and-fire-2018-07-18","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/chronicle-bolas-blood-and-fire-2018-07-18#:~:text=The%20ease%20with%20which,purpose%20was%20surprisingly%20pleasurable.","archived":null,"license":null,"text":"\"Chronicle of Bolas: Blood and Fire\" by Kate Elliott. Magic Story, Wizards of the Coast, 18 Jul 2018."}]},{"text":"In legend she destroyed the townsfolk of Mors Ridge until a stranger's spell brought her down and she was buried.","cites":["palladia-mors-e1"],"links":["https://mtg.wiki/page/Palladia-Mors#:~:text=Palladia%2DMors%20shrieked%20a%20battle,to%20destroy%20the%20humans."],"citations":[{"source":"mtg-wiki","official":false,"publisher":"MTG Wiki contributors","work":"Palladia-Mors","series":"MTG Wiki","authors":[],"date":"","url":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Palladia-Mors","link":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Palladia-Mors#:~:text=Palladia%2DMors%20shrieked%20a%20battle,to%20destroy%20the%20humans.","archived":null,"license":"CC BY-NC-SA 4.0","text":"\"Palladia-Mors\", section \"Legend of Mors Ridge\". MTG Wiki contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0."}]},{"text":"Red Donald's canals awakened her, and she and Vaevictis wreaked havoc with an army of zombies and orcs and killed Red Donald.","cites":